{"name":"Holiday Blue","hex":"#32bcd1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holiday","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A day on which a religious event or secular celebration is traditionally observed.","A day declared free from work by the state or government."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take a period of time away from work or study.","To spend a period of time in recreational travel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holiday"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holiday","blocks":[{"text":"A holiday is a day or other period of time set aside for festivals or recreation. Public holidays are set by public authorities and vary by state or region. Religious holidays are set by religious organizations for their members and are often also observed as public holidays in religious majority countries. Some religious holidays, such as Christmas, have become secularised by part or all of those who observe them. In addition to secularisation, many holidays have become commercialised due to the growth of industry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg/330px-Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holiday","wikidata":"Q1445650"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/500px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/1280px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/500px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChamps-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/500px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/1280px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut